packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:234:  { name: 'host_run', level: 'L2', category: 'managed-provider-execution', owner: 'handlers/host-run + core/managed-host-run', rationale: 'Submits one durable provider CLI execution whose worker, process group, finite absolute deadline, output projection, terminal and receipt outlive the observing caller. The handler mirrors finite-positive-integer timeout/deadline schema constraints and publishes the exact durable runId through progress before foreground attach so a replacement caller can recover without duplicate spawn. For a managed reviewer, the one-shot capability descriptor settles the controller on local write finish (not worker-side descriptor close), then the independent durable claim handshake bounds detached submission without waiting for provider terminal exit. Shared provider admission is mandatory even with usage accounting disabled, and release mutation failures remain observable. Ordinary output/usage remain diagnostic; formal --managedReview derives the exact prompt and immutable story/reviewRun/lane/provider/material tuple, and only the provider adapter bounded final-result lane may produce an unimported proposal. Managed Claude alone receives its mode-0600 one-shot prompt below the exact provider cwd in a sealed runId-bound leaf; normal worker cleanup plus terminal reconciliation/expiry repair remove only that exact leaf after a crash, alongside an explicit non-interactive permission mode and a bounded non-secret JSON Schema bound to the exact managed tuple. Only its successful terminal provider-validated structured_output is proposal input, while prose and fenced JSON fail closed. The detached worker FD selector is removed from the provider environment. Ordinary Claude and Codex launch policy/transport remain unchanged.' },
